=== A: precedence by path order
-pa d1 -pa d2                            -> Json:who()=d2 which=d2/Json.beam
-pa d2 -pa d1                            -> Json:who()=d1 which=d1/Json.beam
-pz d1 -pz d2                            -> Json:who()=d1 which=d1/Json.beam
-pa d1 -pz d2                            -> Json:who()=d1 which=d1/Json.beam
-pz d1 -pa d2                            -> Json:who()=d2 which=d2/Json.beam
=== B: code:clash/0 with both on the path (the tool that reports exactly this)
** d2/Json.beam hides d1/Json.beam
** Found 1 name clashes in code paths 
=== C: both versions loaded in one VM: second load_binary of same name; old-code limit
load1 {module,'Json'}
who after load1: d1
load2 {module,'Json'} (replaces; d1 becomes old code)
who after load2: d2; old code present: true
load3 (third, old code not purged) {module,'Json'}
soft_purge true
